# Data Security / データセキュリティ

## Never Expose Secrets to Client / クライアントに秘密を出さない

The following must **never** appear in client bundles, `NEXT_PUBLIC_*` variables (unless explicitly safe), or browser-accessible API responses:

| Secret Type | Examples |
|---|---|
| Database | Supabase `service_role` key |
| External AI | OpenAI, Anthropic, Tavily, Exa API keys |
| Research | SearXNG admin tokens (if any) |
| Infrastructure | Cron secrets, webhook signing keys |

Use server-side Application Services and Edge Functions for all privileged operations.

## Row-Level Security / 行レベルセキュリティ

- All tenant-scoped tables **must** have RLS enabled in Supabase.
- Policies enforce organization membership and role permissions — never rely on client-side filtering alone.
- See `docs/architecture/rls-matrix.md` and `docs/architecture/permission-matrix.md`.

## Data Flow Rules / データフロー規則

1. Browser → authenticated API route / server action → Application Service → Repository (with user JWT context).
2. Background workers use service role **only** in isolated worker processes, never in Next.js client components.
3. Research providers (SearXNG primary; Tavily/Firecrawl/Exa as fallback interfaces) execute **server-side only**.

## UI Security / UI セキュリティ

- Don't display internal implementation names that aid reconnaissance (provider class names, table names) to general users.
- Error responses: generic message to user, detailed log server-side.
- Audit sensitive actions (permission changes, export, delete) at the Application Service layer.

## Type Safety as Security / 型安全とセキュリティ

- Validate all external input with schemas at service boundaries.
- Avoid `any` on auth context and permission checks — typed roles and capability enums.
- `lint`, `typecheck`, `test`, `build` are mandatory gates before deployment.

## Product Context / プロダクト文脈

Regapro AI is a **business OS** handling customer and deal data. Security failures are business failures — not acceptable tradeoffs for faster AI demos.
